<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#universal-suffrage">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Universal suffrage</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as universal male suffrage</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Universal suffrage is the right of all adult citizens to vote, regardless of property, class or, in its full form, sex. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> introduced universal male suffrage for elections to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> in 1871. Accounts of the German Empire note, however, that real power remained concentrated in the emperor and the chancellor, limiting the democratic effect of this broad franchise.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Pressure for reform grew with modernisation: the Nova Reforma of 1866, the crisis of 1933 that brought <b>universal male suffrage</b>, the vote for women in 1970, and the creation in 1981 of an executive council, whose first head, Òscar Ribas Reig, took office in 1982, gradually separated government…</blockquote><a href="/empire/andorra">Andorra · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>Austria introduced <b>universal male suffrage</b> for the Reichsrat in 1907, while Hungary retained a narrow franchise that entrenched Magyar dominance.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The Reichstag was elected by <b>universal male suffrage</b> and voted the budget, but it could not appoint or remove the chancellor, who remained responsible to the Kaiser alone.</blockquote><a href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>A general strike in 1893 forced <b>universal male suffrage</b> with plural votes for the wealthy and educated, replaced in 1919 by equal male suffrage; women gained the vote in national elections in 1948.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Kingdom of Belgium · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The National Assembly then chose Prince William of Denmark, who reigned as George I from 1863 to 1913 under the constitution of 1864, which established <b>universal male suffrage</b> and a single-chamber parliament.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The suffrage was extended gradually, and the Pacification of 1917 combined <b>universal male suffrage</b> and proportional representation with equal state funding for religious schools, ending the long ‘school struggle’; women gained the vote in 1919.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
